{"path":"3/library/constants.html","title":"Built-in Constants","description":"A small number of constants live in the built-in namespace. They are:","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"anchor","id":"built-in-constants"},{"type":"anchor","id":"built-in-consts"},{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built-in Constants"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A small number of constants live in the built-in namespace. They are:"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"False","term":[{"type":"text","value":"False"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The false value of the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#bool","title":"bool","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"bool"}]},{"type":"text","value":" type. Assignments to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"False"},{"type":"text","value":" are illegal and raise a "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/exceptions.html#SyntaxError","title":"SyntaxError","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"SyntaxError"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"True","term":[{"type":"text","value":"True"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The true value of the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#bool","title":"bool","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"bool"}]},{"type":"text","value":" type. Assignments to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"True"},{"type":"text","value":" are illegal and raise a "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/exceptions.html#SyntaxError","title":"SyntaxError","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"SyntaxError"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"None","term":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An object frequently used to represent the absence of a value, as when default arguments are not passed to a function. Assignments to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"None"},{"type":"text","value":" are illegal and raise a "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/exceptions.html#SyntaxError","title":"SyntaxError","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"SyntaxError"}]},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"None"},{"type":"text","value":" is the sole instance of the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/types.html#types.NoneType","title":"types.NoneType","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"NoneType"}]},{"type":"text","value":" type."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"NotImplemented","term":[{"type":"text","value":"NotImplemented"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A special value which should be returned by the binary special methods (e.g. "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html#object.__eq__","title":"object.__eq__","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"__eq__()"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html#object.__lt__","title":"object.__lt__","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"__lt__()"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html#object.__add__","title":"object.__add__","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"__add__()"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html#object.__rsub__","title":"object.__rsub__","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"__rsub__()"}]},{"type":"text","value":", etc.) to indicate that the operation is not implemented with respect to the other type; may be returned by the in-place binary special methods (e.g. "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html#object.__imul__","title":"object.__imul__","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"__imul__()"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html#object.__iand__","title":"object.__iand__","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"__iand__()"}]},{"type":"text","value":", etc.) for the same purpose. It should not be evaluated in a boolean context. "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"NotImplemented"},{"type":"text","value":" is the sole instance of the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/types.html#types.NotImplementedType","title":"types.NotImplementedType","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"types.NotImplementedType"}]},{"type":"text","value":" type."}]},{"type":"admonition","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When a binary (or in-place) method returns "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"NotImplemented"},{"type":"text","value":" the interpreter will try the reflected operation on the other type (or some other fallback, depending on the operator). If all attempts return "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"NotImplemented"},{"type":"text","value":", the interpreter will raise an appropriate exception. Incorrectly returning "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"NotImplemented"},{"type":"text","value":" will result in a misleading error message or the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"NotImplemented"},{"type":"text","value":" value being returned to Python code."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/numbers.html#implementing-the-arithmetic-operations","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Implementing the arithmetic operations"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for examples."}]}]},{"type":"admonition","kind":"caution","title":"Caution","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"NotImplemented"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"NotImplementedError"},{"type":"text","value":" are not interchangeable. This constant should only be used as described above; see "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/exceptions.html#NotImplementedError","title":"NotImplementedError","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"NotImplementedError"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for details on correct usage of the exception."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changed in version 3.9: Evaluating "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"NotImplemented"},{"type":"text","value":" in a boolean context was deprecated."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changed in version 3.14: Evaluating "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"NotImplemented"},{"type":"text","value":" in a boolean context now raises a "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/exceptions.html#TypeError","title":"TypeError","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"TypeError"}]},{"type":"text","value":". It previously evaluated to "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/constants.html#True","title":"True","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"True"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and emitted a "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/exceptions.html#DeprecationWarning","title":"DeprecationWarning","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"DeprecationWarning"}]},{"type":"text","value":" since Python 3.9."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"Ellipsis","term":[{"type":"text","value":"Ellipsis"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same as the ellipsis literal “"},{"type":"inline_code","code":"..."},{"type":"text","value":"”, an object frequently used to indicate that something is omitted. Assignment to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Ellipsis"},{"type":"text","value":" is possible, but assignment to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"..."},{"type":"text","value":" raises a "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/exceptions.html#SyntaxError","title":"SyntaxError","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"SyntaxError"}]},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Ellipsis"},{"type":"text","value":" is the sole instance of the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/types.html#types.EllipsisType","title":"types.EllipsisType","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"types.EllipsisType"}]},{"type":"text","value":" type."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"debug__","term":[{"type":"text","value":"__debug__"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This constant is true if Python was not started with an "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/using/cmdline.html#cmdoption-O","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"-O"}]},{"type":"text","value":" option. See also the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/simple_stmts.html#assert","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"assert"}]},{"type":"text","value":" statement."}]}]}]},{"type":"admonition","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The names "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/constants.html#None","title":"None","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"None"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/constants.html#False","title":"False","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"False"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/constants.html#True","title":"True","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"True"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/constants.html#debug__","title":"__debug__","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"__debug__"}]},{"type":"text","value":" cannot be reassigned (assignments to them, even as an attribute name, raise "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/exceptions.html#SyntaxError","title":"SyntaxError","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"SyntaxError"}]},{"type":"text","value":"), so they can be considered “true” constants."}]}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"constants-added-by-the-site-module"},{"type":"anchor","id":"site-consts"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Constants added by the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/site.html#module-site","title":"site: Module responsible for site-specific configuration.","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"site"}]},{"type":"text","value":" module"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/site.html#module-site","title":"site: Module responsible for site-specific configuration.","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"site"}]},{"type":"text","value":" module (which is imported automatically during startup, except if the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/using/cmdline.html#cmdoption-S","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"-S"}]},{"type":"text","value":" command-line option is given) adds several constants to the built-in namespace. They are useful for the interactive interpreter shell and should not be used in programs."}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"quit","term":[{"type":"text","value":"quit("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"code"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[]},{"id":"exit","term":[{"type":"text","value":"exit("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"code"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Objects that when printed, print a message like “Use quit() or Ctrl-D (i.e. EOF) to exit”, and when accessed directly in the interactive interpreter or called as functions, raise "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/exceptions.html#SystemExit","title":"SystemExit","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"SystemExit"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with the specified exit code."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"text","value":"help"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Object that when printed, prints the message “Type help() for interactive help, or help(object) for help about object.”, and when accessed directly in the interactive interpreter, invokes the built-in help system (see "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#help","title":"help","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"help()"}]},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"copyright","term":[{"type":"text","value":"copyright"}],"definition":[]},{"id":"credits","term":[{"type":"text","value":"credits"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Objects that when printed or called, print the text of copyright or credits, respectively."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"license","term":[{"type":"text","value":"license"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Object that when printed, prints the message “Type license() to see the full license text”, and when called, displays the full license text in a pager-like fashion (one screen at a time)."}]}]}]}]}}
